{
  "agent": {
    "commands": [
      "kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop -o wide 2>&1; echo \"---\"; kubectl get events -n astronomy-shop --sort-by=.lastTimestamp 2>&1 | tail -40",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get deploy -n astronomy-shop 2>&1; echo \"---RS\"; kubectl get rs -n astronomy-shop 2>&1 | grep -E \"payment|flagd\"; echo \"---rollout\"; kubectl rollout history deploy/payment -n astronomy-shop 2>&1; kubectl rollout history deploy/flagd -n astronomy-shop 2>&1; echo \"---flagd cm\"; kubectl get cm -n astronomy-shop 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get deploy payment -n astronomy-shop -o yaml 2>&1 | sed -n '1,200p'",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get cm flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o yaml 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get deploy flagd -n astronomy-shop -o yaml 2>&1 | sed -n '1,220p'",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl logs deploy/payment -n astronomy-shop --tail=20 2>&1; echo \"---checkout\"; kubectl logs deploy/checkout -n astronomy-shop --tail=10 2>&1; echo \"---flagd\"; kubectl logs deploy/flagd -n astronomy-shop -c flagd --tail=10 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get cm flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o yaml > /tmp/flagd-config.yaml && grep -n '\"defaultVariant\": \"100%\"' /tmp/flagd-config.yaml && sed -i 's/\"defaultVariant\": \"100%\"/\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"/' /tmp/flagd-config.yaml && kubectl apply -f /tmp/flagd-config.yaml 2>&1 && kubectl rollout restart deploy/flagd -n astronomy-shop 2>&1 && kubectl rollout status deploy/flagd -n astronomy-shop --timeout=180s 2>&1",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl get cm flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' 2>&1 | grep -A1 '\"paymentFailure\"' ; kubectl get cm flagd-config -n astronomy-shop -o jsonpath='{.data.demo\\.flagd\\.json}' | grep -c '\"defaultVariant\": \"100%\"'; echo \"--- pod flag file\"; kubectl exec -n astronomy-shop deploy/flagd -c flagd -- sh -c 'grep -A8 paymentFailure ./etc/flagd/demo.flagd.json | grep defaultVariant' 2>&1; echo \"--- pods\"; kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop 2>&1 | grep -vE \"Running\\s+0|1/1|2/2|4/4\" ; kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop -l opentelemetry.io/name=flagd 2>&1; echo \"--- payment logs (recent errors)\"; kubectl logs deploy/payment -n astronomy-shop --since=2m 2>&1 | grep -iE \"error|fail\" | head -5; echo \"(end)\"",
      "cd /tmp; sleep 45; echo \"--- payment errors since fix\"; kubectl logs deploy/payment -n astronomy-shop --since=45s 2>&1 | grep -c \"Invalid token\"; echo \"--- flagd pod live config\"; POD=$(kubectl get pod -n astronomy-shop -l opentelemetry.io/name=flagd -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}'); kubectl exec -n astronomy-shop \"$POD\" -c flagd -- cat ./etc/flagd/demo.flagd.json 2>&1 | grep -A8 '\"paymentFailure\"' | grep defaultVariant; echo \"--- pods\"; kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop 2>&1 | awk 'NR>1 && $2!~/^([0-9]+)\\/\\1$/ || NR==1'"
    ],
    "exit_code": 0,
    "image": "sremut-agent:k8s-1.32",
    "is_error": false,
    "limit_reached": false,
    "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
    "seconds": 80,
    "summary": "The payment failure is fixed: the `paymentFailure` default in the flagd ConfigMap is now `off`, and flagd restarted with that config. No payment \"Invalid token\" errors appeared in the 45 seconds after the fix, and all pods are Running.\n\n**Root cause:** The `flagd-config` ConfigMap set `paymentFailure.defaultVariant` to `\"100%\"`. Every other flag defaults to `off`, so this one made the payment service reject every charge request. The payment logs showed `Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold` errors.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Set `paymentFailure.defaultVariant` from `\"100%\"` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, applied with `kubectl apply`.\n- Ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/flagd`. The flagd init container copies the ConfigMap into the pod only at startup, so the restart was needed for the change to take effect.\n\n**Things to note:**\n- The ConfigMap is managed by Helm (chart `opentelemetry-demo-0.40.4`). A `helm upgrade` will restore the `100%` default unless the flag change is also made in the chart values, which I did not have access to.\n- I could not read the flag file from inside the flagd pod, because the container has no shell. I confirmed the change in the ConfigMap and the flagd rollout, not in the running file.\n- The `accounting` pod restarted once about 48 seconds before my last check. I did not investigate it.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 10,
